"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"remove_edge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"remove_vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), for a directed representation. It exists so that a wrapper which adds a rule, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can own any of the mutable representations as its base and still run at the base’s speed.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}]},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/GraphProtocols/DirectedHypergraph/isBHypergraph":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph\/isBHypergraph","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/graphprotocols\/directedhypergraph\/isbhypergraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether every hyperedge has exactly one target: a B-graph (Gallo et al.‘s backward"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hypergraph; halp’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is_B_hypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":"). Vacuously true with no hyperedges. O(m)."}],"role":"symbol","title":"isBHypergraph","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isBHypergraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/GraphProtocols/DirectedHypergraph/weaklyConnectedComponents()":{"title":"weaklyConnectedComponents()","abstract":[{"text":"The weakly connected components: vertices joined through either side of a chain of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"te